<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>American Food Culture</title>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@700&family=Lato:wght@400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;
      background-color: #FAF8F5;
      color: #002F6C;
    }
    header {
      background-color: #002F6C;
      padding: 1rem 2rem;
      color: white;
      text-align: center;
    }
    header h1 {
      font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .section {
      padding: 2rem;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: auto;
    }
    .section h2 {
      font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
      font-size: 2rem;
      color: #D72638;
    }
    .brand-colors, .typography {
      display: flex;
      gap: 1rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .color-box {
      width: 150px;
      padding: 1rem;
      border-radius: 5px;
      color: white;
      font-weight: bold;
    }
    .Patriotic-Navy { background-color: #002F6C; }
    .Bold-Red { background-color: #D72638; }
    .White { background-color: #FFFFFF; color: #002F6C; border: 1px solid #ccc; }
    .Soft-Cream { background-color: #FAF8F5; color: #002F6C; border: 1px solid #ccc; }
    footer {
      background-color: #002F6C;
      color: white;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 1rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>American Food Culture</h1>
    <p>The Story Behind Every Bite</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Our Story</h2>
    <p>
      We started <strong>American Food Culture</strong> because we were tired of hearing the same thing over and over:
      "America doesn’t have a real food culture." But the truth? That couldn’t be further from reality.
    </p>
    <p>
      American food may not always be refined, but it’s absolutely rich — in stories, history, and influence.
      From ballpark hot dogs to immigrant fusion dishes, food in America reflects struggle, invention, joy,
      rebellion, and identity.
    </p>
    <p>
      We created this platform to:
      <ul>
        <li>🍔 Pay tribute to the foods that shaped our childhoods and communities</li>
        <li>📚 Uncover the wild stories behind iconic dishes</li>
        <li>🎡 Remind people our “guilty pleasures” are cultural artifacts</li>
        <li>🇺🇸 Reframe how the world sees American food — not as a punchline, but a legacy</li>
      </ul>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Brand Identity</h2>
    <h3>Colors</h3>
    <div class="brand-colors">
      <div class="color-box Patriotic-Navy">Patriotic Navy<br>#002F6C</div>
      <div class="color-box Bold-Red">Bold Red<br>#D72638</div>
      <div class="color-box White">White<br>#FFFFFF</div>
      <div class="color-box Soft-Cream">Soft Cream<br>#FAF8F5</div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-top:2rem">Typography</h3>
    <div class="typography">
      <div>
        <strong>Montserrat Bold</strong><br>
        All caps, sans-serif<br>
        <p style="font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight:700;">AMERICAN FOOD CULTURE</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Lato Regular</strong><br>
        Clean sans-serif<br>
        <p style="font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;">The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2025 American Food Culture. All Rights Reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
